      "slug": "samosa-pastry",
      "term": "Samosa pastry",
      "definition": "A thin, unleavened dough made from plain flour, a small amount of fat, and water. It is stiffer than shortcrust pastry, which allows it to be folded into a triangle without cracking and to stay crisp after frying."
    }
